                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fatman's humor and voice acting land well and give it real charm, but the puzzle design is the weak point — several are described as awkward and needlessly obtuse, relying on pixel hunting and the classic early-90s \"walk to/look at/talk to\" action menu that hasn't aged gracefully. On top of that, reviewers note certain screens feel bare and under-detailed, with some interactive objects hard to spot against the background, which only makes the pixel hunting worse. The writing carries the game, but a pass on puzzle logic and object visibility would remove a lot of unnecessary friction for players who aren't already used to adventure games from that era.",
